<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pixodarus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 335 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pixodarus was the youngest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hecatomnus">Hecatomnus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satrapy">satrap</a> of Caria from about 340 to 335 BCE, after ousting his sister Ada. He negotiated a marriage alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a>, which the young Alexander tried to divert to himself. He married his daughter to the Persian Orontobates, who succeeded him shortly before Alexander's invasion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pixodarus.jpg" alt="Pixodarus" width="320" height="366" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG coins · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_on_coinage_of_the_time_of_Pixodaros.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
